{# The button skin as a bare class string, so a <button> that Symfony renders
   can wear the same clothes as the <a> in _button.html.twig without either
   copy drifting from the other. The contrast rule lives here and nowhere
   else: papaya fill with a near-black label, and a hover that LIGHTENS —
   darkening the fill drops the label to 3.43:1.

   Emits no markup. Pull it with include(), assign it, hand it to `attr`.
   Takes no parameters — there is one button, and it looks like this. #}
{%- set base = 'group inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg px-6 py-3.5 font-mono text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] transition-colors' -%}
{{- base ~ ' bg-accent text-neutral-900 hover:bg-accent-hover' -}}
